PREAMBLE

UltraLab is software under development, distributed during a test phase ("alpha") to participants admitted by its author. This license sets out the conditions under which those participants may use it. Subject to the last paragraph of Section 3, it grants no right to any person who has not been admitted to that test phase or who has not accepted this license.


SECTION 1. DEFINITIONS

"Author": the natural person who holds the copyright in the Software, named in the copyright notice at the top of this document and in the NOTICE file of the Software.

"Software": UltraLab in all its forms, including its installers, executables, engine, remote computing station administration program ("Monitor"), processing sequences ("workflows"), prompts sent to language models, configuration files, documentation and updates, excluding Third-party components.

"Third-party components": third-party software and libraries included in or used by the Software, governed by their own licenses.

"Official distribution page": the page where versions of the Software are published in its repository, on its hosting platform, or any other page the Author designates as such.

"Participant": the natural person admitted by the Author to the Alpha program, either by a written notice that names them (email or message) or by the delivery of a personal access code, and who has accepted this license under Section 2. Unless the Author states otherwise in writing, persons who, before September 28, 2026, were using a version of the Software obtained from the Author or from the Official distribution page are also admitted. A contrary notice sent to a person who has already accepted this license ends it under the third paragraph of Section 12.

"Alpha program": the test phase of the Software, which lasts until the end date announced by the Author under Section 12.

"Commercial use": any use of the Software (i) by a company or on its behalf, as part of its profit-making activity, including by a pharmaceutical company, a medical device manufacturer, a contract research provider, a consulting firm or a software publisher; (ii) to provide a third party, for remuneration, with a service, expertise or training; (iii) consisting of selling, renting or reselling the Software, making it available as a service or incorporating it into a product or service. However, use by a Participant for research, study or teaching work carried out alone or as part of a team, within or on behalf of a public or private higher education or research institution, a public or private non-profit healthcare institution, a public administration, a foundation or an association, is not Commercial use, including when the Participant is paid by that organization, when the work is funded by public or private funds, or when it leads to a thesis, a dissertation or a publication, even in a subscription journal. This exception does not apply to work carried out within or on behalf of a pharmaceutical company, a medical device manufacturer, a contract research provider, a consulting firm or a software publisher. In case of doubt, the Participant asks the Author, whose written answer is authoritative.


SECTION 2. ACCEPTANCE

This license is concluded between the Author and the Participant when the Participant, having been able to read it in full, accepts it by clicking the acceptance button of the installer or of the application. The Software records on the Participant's computer the version of the license accepted and the date of acceptance. The text of the license remains available in the application and on the Official distribution page; it can be saved and printed.

Subject to the last paragraph of Section 3, no right is granted without such acceptance. Making the Software available on the Official distribution page does not amount to admission to the Alpha program: a person who is not a Participant acquires no right of use, even if they obtain a copy of the Software or click the acceptance button.


SECTION 3. RIGHTS GRANTED

Under the conditions of this license, the Author grants the Participant, for the term set out in Section 12, a personal, non-exclusive, non-assignable, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free, worldwide right, revocable only under the conditions of Section 12, to:

a) install the Software on the computers they use themselves, where applicable through the IT department of their institution, and on a remote computing station they administer or are authorized to use, provided that only they and, where applicable, other Participants use the Software on those computers;

b) use the Software, excluding any Commercial use, to evaluate it and for their research, study or teaching work, carried out alone or as part of a team;

c) make a backup copy where it is necessary to preserve that use.

The Author claims no rights in the Participant's data or in the results the Participant produces with the Software (corpora, screening decisions, reports, tables, figures, exports, analyses). The Participant may keep, use and publish them freely, including after this license ends, subject to the rights of third parties in the content they include, such as abstracts and articles retrieved from bibliographic databases. Where these results include elements of the Software, in particular the draft "Methods" section, the generated analysis scripts, the settings and prompts sent to the models, the audit log, the reproducibility package or the reviewer pack, the Author authorizes the Participant, free of charge, worldwide and for the full term of the rights, including after this license ends, to reproduce, adapt, publish and communicate them, in particular to their co-authors, reviewers, publishers and readers, to the extent necessary for their work, its publication, its assessment and its reproduction. A person who receives a reviewer pack may use it for the needs of the project for which it was given to them; other recipients of those elements may use them to assess and reproduce that work. This authorization does not allow those elements to be extracted to create other software or another service. A Participant who publishes such work must cite the Software (name and version).


SECTION 4. RESTRICTIONS

Unless the Author has given prior written permission, the Participant shall not:

a) reproduce the Software, in whole or in part, beyond what Section 3 allows;

b) modify, adapt, translate or arrange the Software, create derivative works of it, or reuse all or part of its code, processing sequences, prompts or documentation in any other software or document, subject to the last paragraph of Section 3 and the last paragraph of this Section;

c) share, distribute, lend, rent, sell or make available to anyone a copy of the Software or of its installer, or the personal access code delivered to them under Section 1, including for the benefit of a colleague or their institution, subject to the last paragraph of Section 3; the Participant may, however, refer anyone to the Official distribution page and to the way of applying to join the Alpha program, and give other Participants the pairing codes needed to use a remote computing station under Section 3 a);

d) make any Commercial use of the Software;

e) decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the Software, or circumvent any technical measure protecting it, except where permitted by law (Section 8) or by the license of a Third-party component (Section 7);

f) remove or alter any copyright, license or trademark notice in the Software;

g) use the name "UltraLab" or its logo to designate another product or service, or in a way suggesting that the Author endorses or supports a product, service or publication.

In accordance with paragraph VI of Article L. 122-6-1 and paragraph III of Article L. 122-5-3 of the French Intellectual Property Code, the Author objects to the text and data mining referred to in those provisions being carried out on the Software, including for the purpose of training artificial intelligence systems. This objection covers neither text and data mining carried out for scientific research purposes under the conditions of paragraph II of Article L. 122-5-3, nor the rights the Author has granted to the host of the public repository under that platform's terms of use.

Viewing the public repository of the Software on its hosting platform, within the limits of that platform's terms of use, confers no right to use, reproduce, modify or distribute the Software outside that platform.

Without prejudice to the last paragraph of Section 3, the restrictions above do not prevent the Participant from citing the Software (name, version and address of its Official distribution page) in a publication, report, dissertation or thesis, describing in it the method followed and the settings chosen, and reproducing in it, for scientific transparency and reproducibility, the excerpts of the prompts needed to understand that method, with their source. Using the settings, parameters and customization features provided by the Software, including the rules the Participant adds to the prompts, is not a modification or adaptation under item b).


